<section data-screen-label="What is knee OA" id="what-is-knee-oa" style="background:var(--paper);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:start;margin-bottom:clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Condition context</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">What Is Knee Osteoarthritis?</h2>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Knee osteoarthritis is a whole-joint condition, not simply “worn cartilage.”</strong> It can involve articular cartilage, the bone beneath it, the synovial lining and changes in joint mechanics. Common symptoms include pain, stiffness, swelling and reduced function.</p>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Imaging severity does not always correspond perfectly with symptoms. That is one reason treatment decisions should not be based on an X-ray grade alone. The World Health Organization estimates that knee OA affects roughly 365 million people worldwide.<a href="#ref-14" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">14</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:24px;align-items:stretch">
<figure style="margin:0;position:relative;min-height:360px;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);background:var(--ink-950)">
<img alt="X-ray showing knee osteoarthritis with joint-space narrowing and degenerative changes" loading="lazy" src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/Osteoarthritis_on_X-ray.jpg" style="width:100%;height:100%;min-height:360px;object-fit:cover;display:block;filter:grayscale(1) contrast(1.06);opacity:.88"/>
<figcaption data-dark="true" style="position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;padding:24px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,transparent,oklch(from var(--ink-950) l c h / 0.92));color:var(--white);font-size:12px;line-height:1.6">
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:6px;color:var(--white)">What knee OA can look like on imaging</strong>
            Joint-space narrowing and other structural changes may be visible on X-ray, but imaging severity and symptoms do not always move together.
            <span style="display:block;margin-top:10px;font-size:10px;color:var(--text-on-dark-muted)">Image: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osteoarthritis_on_X-ray.jpg" rel="noopener" target="_blank">James Heilman, MD / Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></span>
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div style="display:grid;gap:24px;align-content:stretch">
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-light)">
<div style="width:46px;height:46px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;background:oklch(from var(--sand-500) l c h / 0.16);color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:20px">
<svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:21px;height:21px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 4c4 1 6 5 5 8s-3 6-2 8"></path><path d="M17 4c-4 1-6 5-5 8s3 6 2 8"></path><path d="M8 11h8"></path></svg>
</div>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:19px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;color:var(--ink-950)">Why this matters for regenerative treatment</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A treatment does not need to regrow cartilage to improve symptoms, and an improvement in pain does not prove that joint structure has been restored.</p>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-light)">
<div style="width:46px;height:46px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;background:oklch(from var(--sand-500) l c h / 0.16);color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:20px">
<svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:21px;height:21px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"></circle><path d="m8.5 12 2.2 2.2L15.8 9"></path></svg>
</div>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:19px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;color:var(--ink-950)">Why diagnosis comes first</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Knee pain can reflect OA, meniscal pathology, instability, alignment problems or other conditions. A biologic treatment should follow diagnosis rather than replace it.</p>
</article>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-screen-label="What stem cell therapy means" id="what-is-stem-cell-therapy" style="background:var(--white);border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:start;margin-bottom:clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">The first buying decision</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">What Does “Stem Cell Therapy for Knees” Actually Mean?</h2>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>“Stem cell therapy” is not one standardized treatment.</strong> Two clinics can both advertise stem cell therapy for knee osteoarthritis while offering biologically different products with different evidence, processing and regulatory requirements.</p>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Stanford and Hospital for Special Surgery both emphasize the importance of distinguishing orthobiologic products rather than treating every intervention as interchangeable “stem cells.”<a href="#ref-15" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">15</a><a href="#ref-16" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">16</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(max(230px,33.33% - 1px),1fr));gap:1px;background:var(--line-on-light);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden">
<div style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);border-top:3px solid var(--sand-500)">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:20px">
<div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--ink-950);background:oklch(from var(--sand-500) l c h / 0.18)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:24px;height:24px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 3h6M10 3v5l-4 8a3 3 0 0 0 3 5h6a3 3 0 0 0 3-5l-4-8V3"></path><path d="M8 15h8"></path></svg></div>
<span style="font-size:9.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--sand-500);white-space:nowrap">Cell-based</span>
</div>
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:8px">BMAC</strong>
<span style="display:block;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Concentrated bone marrow containing multiple cell populations and biological components; not purified or culture-expanded MSC therapy.</span>
</div>
<div style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);border-top:3px solid var(--sand-500)">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:20px">
<div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--ink-950);background:oklch(from var(--sand-500) l c h / 0.18)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:24px;height:24px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="9" cy="9" r="4"></circle><circle cx="16" cy="8" r="2.5"></circle><circle cx="14" cy="16" r="3"></circle></svg></div>
<span style="font-size:9.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--sand-500);white-space:nowrap">Cell-based</span>
</div>
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:8px">Adipose / SVF</strong>
<span style="display:block;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A heterogeneous cell-rich preparation derived from fat tissue; distinct from culture-expanded adipose MSCs.</span>
</div>
<div style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);border-top:3px solid var(--sand-500)">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:20px">
<div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--ink-950);background:oklch(from var(--sand-500) l c h / 0.18)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:24px;height:24px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="8" cy="9" r="3"></circle><circle cx="16" cy="9" r="3"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="17" r="3"></circle></svg></div>
<span style="font-size:9.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--sand-500);white-space:nowrap">Cell-based</span>
</div>
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:8px">Culture-expanded MSCs</strong>
<span style="display:block;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Selected mesenchymal stromal cells expanded under laboratory manufacturing conditions before administration.</span>
</div>
<div style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);border-top:3px solid var(--sand-500)">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:20px">
<div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--ink-950);background:oklch(from var(--sand-500) l c h / 0.18)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:24px;height:24px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="7"></circle><path d="M3 12h6M7 9l-2.5 3L7 15"></path></svg></div>
<span style="font-size:9.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--sand-500);white-space:nowrap">Cell-based</span>
</div>
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:8px">Allogeneic / donor MSCs</strong>
<span style="display:block;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Donor-derived cell products with different manufacturing, immunological and regulatory considerations.</span>
</div>
<div style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);border-top:3px solid var(--line-on-light-strong)">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:20px">
<div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--text-on-light-muted);background:var(--paper)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:24px;height:24px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3c4 5 6 8 6 11a6 6 0 0 1-12 0c0-3 2-6 6-11z"></path><path d="M9 14h6"></path></svg></div>
<span style="font-size:9.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-on-light-muted);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);white-space:nowrap">Not stem cells</span>
</div>
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:8px">PRP</strong>
<span style="display:block;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Concentrated platelets from blood. It is regenerative medicine, but it is not a stem-cell treatment.</span>
</div>
<div style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);border-top:3px solid var(--line-on-light-strong)">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:20px">
<div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--text-on-light-muted);background:var(--paper)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.6" style="width:24px;height:24px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="7" cy="8" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="14" cy="6" r="1.3"></circle><circle cx="17" cy="13" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="9" cy="14" r="1.2"></circle><circle cx="14" cy="18" r="1.4"></circle><circle cx="5" cy="17" r="1.2"></circle></svg></div>
<span style="font-size:9.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-on-light-muted);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);white-space:nowrap">Not stem cells</span>
</div>
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950);margin-bottom:8px">Exosomes / EVs</strong>
<span style="display:block;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Cell-derived extracellular products. They are not live stem cells and should not be presented as the same therapy.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:24px;border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between">
<div style="max-width:60ch">
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Already received a treatment proposal?</strong>
<p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">The label alone is not enough. Product identity, processing, dose, evidence and physician rationale all need to be compared.</p>
</div>
<button class="sc-inline-cta on-light" data-stemcierge-quiz="true" type="button">Help Me Compare Treatment Types</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-screen-label="Does it work" id="does-it-work" style="background:var(--paper);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:start;margin-bottom:clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Effectiveness</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">Does Stem Cell Therapy Work for Knee Osteoarthritis?</h2>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>The best available evidence suggests that some cell-based treatments may provide modest improvements in knee OA pain and function, although results vary by product and study design.</strong> The strongest high-level evidence supports cautious optimism rather than blanket effectiveness claims.</p>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A 2025 Cochrane living review included 25 randomized trials and 1,341 participants. Compared with placebo, stem-cell injections may improve pain by about 1.2 points on a 0–10 scale and function by about 14.2 points on a 0–100 scale at around six months, but Cochrane rated the evidence as low certainty.<a href="#ref-1" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">1</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence">
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__top">
<span class="sc-editorial-evidence__kicker">Cochrane 2025 · ~6-month outcomes</span>
<span class="sc-editorial-evidence__meta">25 RCTs · 1,341 participants · low-certainty evidence<a class="sc-editorial-evidence__cite" href="#ref-1">1</a></span>
</div>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__layout">
<article class="sc-editorial-evidence__takeaway">
<span class="sc-editorial-evidence__mini">Editorial takeaway</span>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__statement">
<span>Modest average</span>
<strong>improvement</strong>
</div>
<p>
        Compared with placebo, the pooled evidence suggests that cell-based injections may provide
        <strong>additional improvement in pain and function</strong> for some people with knee osteoarthritis.
      </p>
<p class="sc-editorial-evidence__context">
        The results support <strong>cautious optimism</strong>, while reinforcing why the exact biological product,
        protocol and patient matter when comparing treatment options.
      </p>
</article>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__metrics">
<article class="sc-editorial-evidence__metric">
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__metric-head">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="sc-editorial-evidence__icon">
<svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.7" viewbox="0 0 24 24">
<path d="M3 13h4l2.5-6 3 12 2.5-6h6"></path>
</svg>
</span>
<span>Pain</span>
</div>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__number">1.2</div>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__number-label">points better vs placebo</div>
<p>Average additional improvement on a <strong>0–10 pain scale</strong>.</p>
</article>
<article class="sc-editorial-evidence__metric">
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__metric-head">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="sc-editorial-evidence__icon">
<svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.7" viewbox="0 0 24 24">
<path d="M5 20V10"></path>
<path d="M12 20V4"></path>
<path d="M19 20v-6"></path>
</svg>
</span>
<span>Function</span>
</div>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__number">14.2</div>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__number-label">points better vs placebo</div>
<p>Average additional improvement on a <strong>0–100 function scale</strong>.</p>
</article>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sc-editorial-evidence__bottom">
<strong>How to read this:</strong>
    These are average differences versus placebo, not “12% effective” or “14% effective.”
    They describe symptom outcomes and should not be interpreted as evidence that cartilage was regenerated.
  </div>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:24px;align-items:start">
<div style="display:grid;gap:1px;background:var(--line-on-light);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden">
<article style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(22px,2.6vw,28px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px 20px;align-items:start">
<span style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--sand-500);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:17px;line-height:1">01</span>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:baseline">
<h3 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:var(--ink-950)">2026 network meta-analysis: statistical improvement was not the whole story</h3>
<span style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">Below MCID</span>
</div>
<p style="grid-column:2;margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Across 24 randomized studies and 2,960 patients, several orthobiologics performed statistically better than hyaluronic acid, but none exceeded the analysis's prespecified minimal clinically important difference for pain or function.<a href="#ref-2" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">2</a></p>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(22px,2.6vw,28px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px 20px;align-items:start">
<span style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--sand-500);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:17px;line-height:1">02</span>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:baseline">
<h3 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:var(--ink-950)">MILES: three cell-based approaches did not outperform corticosteroid</h3>
<span style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">Not superior</span>
</div>
<p style="grid-column:2;margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">In 480 patients with KL grade II–IV OA, BMAC, adipose SVF and donor umbilical-tissue MSCs were not superior to corticosteroid on the main one-year pain outcomes; MRI OA scores did not significantly improve.<a href="#ref-3" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">3</a></p>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(22px,2.6vw,28px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px 20px;align-items:start">
<span style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--sand-500);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:17px;line-height:1">03</span>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:baseline">
<h3 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:var(--ink-950)">A positive phase III trial: symptoms improved, cartilage did not clearly change</h3>
<span style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">Symptoms, not structure</span>
</div>
<p style="grid-column:2;margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A 261-patient trial of culture-expanded autologous adipose MSCs reported better pain and WOMAC scores than placebo, but no significant difference in MRI cartilage-defect change.<a href="#ref-4" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">4</a></p>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);padding:clamp(22px,2.6vw,28px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px 20px;align-items:start">
<span style="width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--sand-500);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:17px;line-height:1">04</span>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:baseline">
<h3 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:var(--ink-950)">ADIPOA2: another adipose-MSC trial was negative</h3>
<span style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">Negative trial</span>
</div>
<p style="grid-column:2;margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">The 2025 phase 2b trial did not show significant superiority over saline placebo on its primary pain/function responder outcome.<a href="#ref-5" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">5</a></p>
</article>
</div>
<aside data-dark="true" style="background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--white);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,36px);position:sticky;top:140px;align-self:start;max-height:calc(100vh - 160px);overflow:auto">
<span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-500)">A useful patient test</span>
<blockquote style="margin:20px 0 0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(22px,2.2vw,28px);line-height:1.28;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--white)">“Did the study find a difference?” and “Would I feel enough better for treatment to be worthwhile?” are not the same question.</blockquote>
<p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">A credible clinic should be able to explain both statistical findings and realistic patient-level expectations.</p>
<div style="margin-top:26px">
<button class="sc-inline-cta on-dark" data-stemcierge-quiz="true" type="button">See Whether This May Be Worth Exploring</button>
</div>
</aside>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="sc-early-bridge" data-screen-label="Why comparison matters">
<div class="sc-early-bridge__inner">
<div class="sc-early-bridge__box">
<div>
<span class="sc-early-bridge__label">Why this gets difficult</span>
<h3>If every knee stem-cell treatment were identical, comparing clinics would be easy.</h3>
<p>They aren't. Cell source, processing, dose, diagnosis, OA severity, physician experience and regulatory environment can all differ. That is why STEMCIERGE helps patients compare the treatment itself before comparing the marketing around it.</p>
</div>
<button class="sc-inline-cta on-light" data-stemcierge-quiz="true" type="button">See Whether This May Be Worth Exploring</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-dark="true" data-screen-label="Evidence framework" id="research-framework" style="background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--white);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-500)">STEMCIERGE evidence framework</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;max-width:24ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--white)">The 5 Questions Behind Every “Stem Cell” Study</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;max-width:70ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:18px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">When studies appear to disagree, these five questions usually explain much of the difference. We use this framework to separate marketing labels from clinically meaningful evidence.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:24px;margin-top:clamp(32px,4vw,48px)">
<article style="border-top:1px solid var(--sand-500);padding:22px 0 0">
<span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--sand-500)">01</span>
<h3 style="margin:16px 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--white)">What product?</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">BMAC, SVF, expanded MSCs and donor-derived products are not interchangeable.</p>
</article>
<article style="border-top:1px solid var(--sand-500);padding:22px 0 0">
<span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--sand-500)">02</span>
<h3 style="margin:16px 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--white)">Which patients?</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">OA severity, alignment, symptoms and treatment history can materially change the population studied.</p>
</article>
<article style="border-top:1px solid var(--sand-500);padding:22px 0 0">
<span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--sand-500)">03</span>
<h3 style="margin:16px 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--white)">Compared with what?</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">Placebo, corticosteroid, HA and another orthobiologic answer different scientific questions.</p>
</article>
<article style="border-top:1px solid var(--sand-500);padding:22px 0 0">
<span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--sand-500)">04</span>
<h3 style="margin:16px 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--white)">Which outcome?</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">Pain, function, MRI structure and disease progression should not be blended together.</p>
</article>
<article style="border-top:1px solid var(--sand-500);padding:22px 0 0">
<span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--sand-500)">05</span>
<h3 style="margin:16px 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--white)">Clinically meaningful?</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">A statistically significant result may still be too small for the average patient to consider worthwhile.</p>
</article>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-screen-label="Cartilage expectations" id="cartilage" style="background:var(--paper);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Expectation setting</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;max-width:26ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">Pain Relief Is Not the Same as Cartilage Regeneration</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;max-width:70ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:18px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">One of the most important questions is not simply whether symptoms improve, but what kind of outcome has actually been demonstrated. The four outcomes below are ordered from most to least often demonstrated in trials.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(210px,1fr));gap:24px;margin-top:clamp(32px,4vw,48px)">
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:26px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:18px">
<span style="width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);border:1px solid var(--sand-500);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--sand-700)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.5" style="width:18px;height:18px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M20 12H4"></path><path d="M8 8l-4 4 4 4"></path></svg></span>
<span style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:15px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">01</span>
</div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:16px;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--sand-500)">Frequently shown</span>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Pain relief</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Your knee hurts less. This can be valuable even without structural repair.</p>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:26px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:18px">
<span style="width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);border:1px solid var(--sand-500);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--sand-700)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.5" style="width:18px;height:18px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 20l4-7 4 3 4-9"></path><path d="M4 20h16"></path></svg></span>
<span style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:15px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">02</span>
</div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:16px;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--sand-500)">Often shown</span>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Better function</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Walking, stairs, sport or everyday activities become easier.</p>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:26px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:18px">
<span style="width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.5" style="width:18px;height:18px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 19V9l8-5 8 5v10"></path><path d="M9 19v-6h6v6"></path></svg></span>
<span style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:15px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">03</span>
</div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:16px;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-on-light-muted);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong)">Rarely shown</span>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Structural change</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Imaging or tissue structure measurably changes.</p>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:26px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:18px">
<span style="width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="1.5" style="width:18px;height:18px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 18c4 0 5-12 9-12s3 8 7 8"></path></svg></span>
<span style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:15px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)">04</span>
</div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:16px;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-on-light-muted);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong)">Not established</span>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Disease modification</h3>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">The underlying progression of osteoarthritis is meaningfully altered.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div data-dark="true" style="margin-top:24px;background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--white);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(24px,3vw,36px);align-items:center">
<div style="width:clamp(120px,15vw,180px);height:clamp(120px,15vw,180px);border-radius:50%;overflow:hidden;flex:0 0 auto;padding:3px;border:1px solid oklch(from var(--sand-500) l c h / 0.55)">
<div class="sc-original-visual-slot is-circle" id="knee-cartilage-cross-section"><span class="slot-label">Visual placeholder</span><strong>Close-up: knee joint cartilage cross-section or MRI detail</strong><small>Replace with a final editorial image or purpose-built infographic before publishing.</small></div>
</div>
<div>
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:var(--white);margin-bottom:14px">Can stem cells regrow knee cartilage?</strong>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:78ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">Routine intra-articular stem-cell or cell-based injections have not been shown to reliably regenerate durable normal knee cartilage. Cochrane remains uncertain about structural progression, MILES did not show significant MRI OA-score improvement, and a positive adipose-MSC trial improved symptoms without a significant difference in MRI cartilage-defect change.<a href="#ref-1" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">1</a><a href="#ref-3" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">3</a><a href="#ref-4" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">4</a></p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 0;max-width:78ch;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-dark-muted)">Surgical cartilage-restoration procedures and tissue-engineering approaches are a different category and should not be confused with a simple intra-articular injection.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
